Next, for the second method, I'll consider breaking down each fraction into its components according to the rules of adding fractions. This might involve understanding how to adjust each fraction so they share the same denominator without necessarily calculating the LCM right away, but instead using multiplication factors to scale both fractions appropriately. It's important to make sure that both fractions are adjusted correctly before performing the addition.

